10791	{"artifactId":"LLD-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330-s2","entry":{"id":"review-f2e2bdb0f30cca110ea2fe0084b68606","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:18:32.965Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's scope covers exactly s2's acceptance criteria (ac1-ac4: explicit resume preserving completed tasks, sequential re-review with history, terminal tasks never silently retried, CR refresh with provenance) and does not build s1's or s3's owned work (normal entrypoint/session integration, approval-triggered checkpoint cleanup, the version-2 CR writer itself).","evidence":"DEF-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json s2.acceptanceCriteria ac1-ac4 match the LLD's §7 acceptance-mapping rows verbatim in intent. The LLD's §8 migration explicitly states 'Keep the normal entrypoints, legacy routing and cleanup policy unchanged until S3' and 'No public normal-workflow endpoint changes are introduced in S2', and src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts today hard-codes `attempt === 1` ('Fresh reviewId and attempt=1 required'), confirming the RPC/session layer the LLD leaves alone is indeed untouched S1/S3 territory. [files: /.insrc/artifacts/DEF-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json, src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Migration §8 'State before' claims S1 is fresh-attempt-only at both the coordinator and RPC layers, with no recovery implementation.","evidence":"coordinator.ts admit(): `requireReview(attempt === 1, 'attempt', 'Fresh first attempts only; recovery is not implemented here')`; task-review-rpc.ts startTaskReview(): `requireReview(typeof p['reviewId'] === 'string' && p['attempt'] === 1, 'request', 'Fresh reviewId and attempt=1 required')`. No resume code path exists anywhere in coordinator.ts/controller.ts today. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts, src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Migration §8 claims 'Terminal results are already saved atomically and publication is already idempotent.'","evidence":"checkpoint.ts saveCheckpoint() writes to a random temp file then renames (atomic replace) with fsync on file and directory. publication.ts mergeTaskSummary()/publishTaskCheckpoint() reject a conflicting same-attempt republish via `isDeepStrictEqual(existing, summary)` and otherwise return the already-merged body unchanged, which is idempotent replay. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/checkpoint.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/record.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"§2.2 claims `publishTaskCheckpoint(project, epicHash, reviewId, deps)` is the existing function being reused (unchanged signature), per its 'Keep... reused' framing and the sharedContracts note that sc3 is already owned/implemented by s1.","evidence":"The real exported function is `export async function publishTaskCheckpoint(project: string, epicHash:string, reviewId:string, deps:PublicationDeps):Promise<{ path:string; jsonPath:string; status:string }>` in publication.ts — parameter order, names and return shape match the LLD's contract exactly. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"§3.1 lists the call sites of `ReviewCheckpoint` as exactly `src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts`, `coordinator.ts`, `controller.ts`, `publication.ts`.","evidence":"Grepping the real source for `ReviewCheckpoint` shows it is referenced in coordinator.ts, checkpoint.ts, controller.ts, execution.ts, publication.ts and contracts.ts — but NOT in src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts (that file never imports or names `ReviewCheckpoint`; it only calls coordinator/publication functions by name). The listed inventory both includes a file that is not a call site and omits two real ones (checkpoint.ts, execution.ts), which matters because execution.ts's `completeReview`/`persistReview` and checkpoint.ts's path/save helpers are exactly the shared plumbing a resume implementation must route through. [files: src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/checkpoint.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/execution.ts]","action":"Correct the §3.1 call-site list to add checkpoint.ts and execution.ts and drop task-review-rpc.ts (or justify why task-review-rpc.ts is listed despite not referencing the type).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"§3.2/§3.4 describe `header.reassessmentSummary`, `review-response.origins` and the CR summary's `origins`/`reassessmentSummary` as additive optional fields that old schema1 checkpoints and schema2 CRs remain readable without, and migration §8 promises no data rewrite.","evidence":"The real validators (`CheckpointSchema` in publication.ts, `SummarySchema`/`TaskBodySchema` in record.ts) are TypeBox objects with `additionalProperties:false`, so decoding old data that lacks the new fields against a schema where the new fields are declared `Type.Optional(...)` succeeds unchanged — exactly the additive pattern the LLD assumes, and both files are correctly named as call sites that must carry the schema edit. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/record.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD extends `ReviewCheckpoint`/`ReviewAttempt`/`TaskReviewResult`/`CompletedReviewSummary`, all tagged `ownedByStory: s1` in the HLD's sharedContracts, which could be a redesign of another story's owned contract.","evidence":"HLD body.rolloutOverview explicitly assigns this exact work to Phase B / story s2 ('Add interrupted-task recovery and history-aware later attempts only after the basic review path proves useful... Retain prior attempt inputs/results and recognize the new checkpoint schema explicitly'), and HLD sc2's own interfaceSketch already anticipates an `operation: 'start' | 'resume'` field on `ReviewRequest`. The s2 LLD's changes are purely additive (new optional fields, no removal/narrowing of s1's existing shapes) and s2's own 'Adjacent scope' section correctly refrains from touching s1's RPC entrypoint or s3's session/cleanup scope, so this is the anticipated additive evolution the HLD planned for this story, not an undocumented redesign. [files: /.insrc/artifacts/HLD-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"§2.1's Errors (`already-running`, `attempt-conflict`, `missing-checkpoint`, `wrong-reviewer`) and §6's detection/response steps build on existing error codes/mechanisms rather than inventing an incompatible new taxonomy.","evidence":"coordinator.ts already throws `already-running` and `attempt-conflict: checkpoint already exists` in admit(), and its private `controller()` helper already throws `missing-checkpoint`/`wrong-reviewer` via `requireReview`. These match the HLD sc2 `ReviewError` union exactly, so the LLD's resume-specific branching (same codes, new triggering conditions) is a coherent extension of a real, already-wired error path rather than a fabricated one. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"§7's acceptance-mapping table maps every DEF s2 acceptance criterion (ac1-ac4, read from DEF-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json) to at least one named test subject.","evidence":"DEF s2 ac1 ('explicit retrigger... preserves completed task results, restarts only unfinished work, no automatic daemon-startup resume'), ac2 (sequential new attempt with stable review-id and full history), ac3 (terminal task never retried same-attempt) and ac4 (correct attempt metadata + CR refresh without presenting old feedback as new) each have at least one plausibly-matching row in the LLD's acceptance-mapping table, and the named test files (coordinator.test.ts, controller.test.ts, publication.test.ts) exist and use `node:test`/`node:assert` as claimed. [files: /.insrc/artifacts/DEF-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/coordinator.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/controller.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/publication.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac4's specific clause ('the returned metadata and checkpoint identify the correct attempt') is covered by a named test subject, not just the CR-refresh half of ac4.","evidence":"ac4 is mapped only to 'publication recovery...', 'old checkpoint and CR compatibility...' and 'S2 deployability...' — all about CR projection/compat/build-health, not explicitly about the controller/coordinator frame returning the correct attempt number on a retrigger. No test subject in §7 is titled around attempt-metadata correctness on retrigger, and I found no way to confirm from the design text alone whether this half of ac4 is exercised by one of the listed subjects implicitly or is simply unnamed.","action":"Name an explicit test subject for 'retrigger returns the correct attempt/status metadata' under ac4, or clarify which existing subject already covers it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":9,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-31T19:18:32.965Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
