13209	{"artifactId":"LLD-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330-s2","entry":{"id":"review-61a20b86b67b1ebee65e603c466f040a","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:24:24.173Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of the Story's acceptance criteria (ac1: explicit resume skips completed tasks and never auto-resumes on daemon startup; ac2: sequential re-review with stable review-id and full prior history; ac3: terminal failed/incomplete tasks are not retried in the same attempt; ac4: returned metadata/CR correctly label reused vs fresh feedback) is addressed by a specific LLD mechanism (resume Preconditions/Postconditions in §2.1, the attribution-with-history flow in §3.3, and the CR origins/reassessmentSummary fields in §3.4) and by the §7 acceptance-mapping table.","evidence":"DEF-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json lines 249-291 list ac1-ac4 verbatim matching the LLD's 'ac1'..'ac4' in §7's acceptance mapping table, and §2.1/§3.3/§3.4 directly implement each 'given/when/then'. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json]","action":"Read DEF-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json acceptance criteria for s2 and cross-checked against LLD §2.1, §3.3, §3.4, §7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD builds nothing from the explicitly-excluded adjacent scope (s1's first-pass flow already exists; s3's normal entrypoint integration, concurrency dedup and story-approval checkpoint cleanup).","evidence":"The LLD's own call-site lists (contracts.ts, coordinator.ts, checkpoint.ts, controller.ts, execution.ts, publication.ts, assessment.ts, results.ts, policy.ts, record.ts, completion.ts) contain no entrypoint/session-integration or cleanup files; completion.ts:7 explicitly comments 'Approval events and checkpoint cleanup remain S3.' [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/completion.ts]","action":"Read completion.ts and grepped the repo for cleanup/unlink/checkpoint-deletion logic.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today's coordinator only admits a fresh first attempt and has no resume path — matching the LLD's 'State before' claim of 'S1 fresh-attempt-only coordinator/RPC admission.'","evidence":"coordinator.ts:74 `requireReview(attempt === 1, 'attempt', 'Fresh first attempts only; recovery is not implemented here');` and admit() unconditionally rejects an existing checkpoint file (line 80). [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts]","action":"Read coordinator.ts admit().","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A controller disconnect today marks the attempt interrupted but there is no implemented way to resume it — matching the claim 'controller reconnection currently requires an explicit retrigger but no recovery implementation exists.'","evidence":"controller.ts:128-131 `stop()` sets `header.interrupted=true` and persists, then `retire(true)`; there is no coordinator/controller method that reopens an interrupted attempt (admit() always requires attempt===1 with no existing file). [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/controller.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts]","action":"Read controller.ts stop()/retire() and cross-checked coordinator.ts admit().","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"`TaskReviewCoordinator.start` and `publishTaskCheckpoint`, described as existing surfaces being extended, exist today with the stated shape (publishTaskCheckpoint's signature matches exactly).","evidence":"coordinator.ts:40 `async start(project, reviewId, attempt, input, context?)`; publication.ts:24 `export async function publishTaskCheckpoint(project: string, epicHash:string, reviewId:string, deps:PublicationDeps):Promise<{ path:string; jsonPath:string; status:string }>` — identical to LLD §2.2's declared signature and return type. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts]","action":"Read coordinator.ts and publication.ts signatures and compared to LLD §2.1/§2.2.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"`origins` on review-response/CR summary and `header.reassessmentSummary` are genuinely new optional fields, not already present in the current contracts.","evidence":"contracts.ts:69-76 defines `ReviewAttempt.header` (attempt/reviewer/status/createdAt/completedAt/activeTaskId/interrupted/selectedTaskIds/buildFingerprint) and `review-response` (summary/tasks/crPath/crPublication/error) with no `reassessmentSummary` or `origins` fields, and `CompletedReviewSummary` (line 74-77) has no `origins` field either. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts]","action":"Read contracts.ts interface definitions for ReviewAttempt and CompletedReviewSummary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The five call sites listed for the `ReviewCheckpoint` invariant-change (coordinator.ts, checkpoint.ts, controller.ts, execution.ts, publication.ts) are real files that would need to accept >1 attempt in the attempts array.","evidence":"All five files exist (`src/workflow/code-review/task-review/{coordinator,checkpoint,controller,execution,publication}.ts`), and checkpoint.ts/contracts.ts already model `attempts: readonly ReviewAttempt[]` as an array (contracts.ts:73), so the structural extension point is correctly identified. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/checkpoint.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts]","action":"Globbed the task-review directory and read checkpoint.ts/contracts.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The call sites listed for `TaskReviewResult`'s invariant-change (assessment.ts, results.ts, policy.ts, coordinator.ts, controller.ts) are exactly the files that currently build/validate task assignments and results, so the new reassess/reuse decision has a correct landing spot.","evidence":"assessment.ts defines AttributionSchema/attributionPrompt/assessTaskResult; policy.ts defines assignmentPrompt/TASK_REVIEW_POLICY; results.ts defines validateTaskResult/normalizeTaskResult — all consumed from coordinator.ts/controller.ts's task loop, matching the described extension points. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/assessment.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/policy.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/results.ts]","action":"Read assessment.ts, policy.ts, results.ts and traced their use from coordinator.ts/controller.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Old schema1 checkpoints and schema2 CR records with no origin/reassessmentSummary fields remain readable, because the validators treat these as optional additions rather than required fields, and existing merge/read logic (`mergeTaskSummary`, `validateTaskBody`, `latestReviewSummaries`) is shape-driven rather than version-switched beyond the existing v1/v2 discriminators.","evidence":"record.ts's `mergeTaskSummary` (lines 44-58) and `validateTaskBody` (lines 28-43) decode via TypeBox schemas keyed on `format`/`kind`/`schemaVersion`, with no field required beyond what's already in `SummarySchema`/`TaskBodySchema` — adding optional fields to those schemas (as the LLD's call-site lists for record.ts/publication.ts/contracts.ts/completion.ts specify) is additive and does not break reading old records that omit them. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/record.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts]","action":"Read record.ts mergeTaskSummary/validateTaskBody and publication.ts's CheckpointSchema to confirm the additive-optional-field pattern is structurally compatible.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"None of this LLD's contract/call-site changes touch files or responsibilities the HLD assigns to s1 (already-built first-pass flow) or s3 (normal entrypoint/session integration, concurrency dedup, story-approval checkpoint cleanup).","evidence":"HLD storyBoundaries (HLD-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json lines 121-151) assign s3 'concurrency/approval cleanup verification ... delete only checkpoint files whose canonical story identity matches that BUILD'; the LLD's own §1 'Adjacent scope' section quotes this s3 description verbatim as do-not-implement-here, and no file in the LLD's call-site lists (e.g. no daemon entrypoint/session file, no cleanup/deletion logic) falls under that scope. [files: .insrc/artifacts/HLD-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/completion.ts]","action":"Read HLD-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330.json storyBoundaries and compared against every call-site file listed in LLD §3 and the completion.ts 'remains S3' comment.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The error codes the LLD's §2.1 catalog relies on (`already-running`, `missing-checkpoint`, `wrong-reviewer`, and the general 'attempt-conflict' family) already exist as concrete thrown errors in the coordinator/controller, so extending them for resume semantics is grounded in real code, not invented.","evidence":"coordinator.ts:75 `requireReview(!this.active.has(path), 'reviewId', 'already-running')`; line 80 `'reviewId', 'attempt-conflict: checkpoint already exists'`; coordinator.ts:67-68 `'checkpoint', ...'missing-checkpoint'...` and `'reviewer','wrong-reviewer'`. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts]","action":"Read coordinator.ts's admit() and controller() methods for the exact error strings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'history cannot fit existing bounded JSON or provider context' error path is grounded in a real existing size cap that resume history would also have to pass.","evidence":"contracts.ts:38-45 `decodeReview` enforces `Buffer.byteLength(bytes) <= 4 * 1024 * 1024` and throws `TaskReviewInputError('input','Expected bounded JSON')` on overflow — the same path a growing multi-attempt checkpoint would hit. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts]","action":"Read contracts.ts decodeReview().","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test files the LLD's §7 cites as the existing framework evidence (coordinator.test.ts, controller.test.ts, publication.test.ts, using node:test/tsx) actually exist in the repo at the stated location.","evidence":"Glob of `src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/*.test.ts` returns contracts.test.ts, publication.test.ts, controller.test.ts, policy.test.ts, coordinator.test.ts — all three cited files are present. [files: src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/coordinator.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/controller.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/publication.test.ts]","action":"Globbed the __tests__ directory.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every acceptance criterion (ac1-ac4) in the §7 mapping table has at least one named proving test subject, with no criterion left unmapped.","evidence":"The §7 'Acceptance mapping' table lists a non-empty 'Proving tests' cell for each of ac1, ac2, ac3 and ac4, drawing from the unit/integration/smoke subjects declared earlier in §7 (e.g. 'interrupted recovery: only absent tasks rerun...', 'sequential re-review: full history in attribution...').","action":"Re-read the LLD §7 acceptance-mapping table against the declared test subjects.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-31T19:24:24.173Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
